.TH ACC-WEBGUI 1 2026-10-22 "ACC" "ACC Manual"
.SH NAME
acc-webgui \- web UI and HTTP API for ACC collectives
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B acc-webgui
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B acc-webgui
serves the ACC web UI: a REST and WebSocket API over the collectives it
observes on the NATS bus, and the compiled single-page application that
uses it.
When the package carries no compiled UI it serves the API alone.
An OpenAI-compatible endpoint may be mounted at \fI/v1\fR.
.PP
The command takes no arguments; it is configured through the environment.
It binds \fB127.0.0.1:8080\fR by default and
.B refuses to start
on any other address unless an authentication mode is configured: an
unauthenticated UI is never exposed on the network.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BR ACC_WEBGUI_HOST ", " ACC_WEBGUI_PORT
The bind address (default \fB127.0.0.1\fR) and port (default \fB8080\fR).
.TP
.B ACC_NATS_URL
The bus (default \fBnats://localhost:4222\fR).
.TP
.BR ACC_COLLECTIVE_IDS ", " ACC_COLLECTIVE_ID
The collectives to observe, comma-separated, or a single one.
.TP
.B ACC_WEBGUI_AUTH_MODE
How users authenticate: \fBoauth\-proxy\fR, \fBoidc\fR, \fBhtpasswd\fR,
\fBmtls\fR or \fBtoken\fR.
Unset means none, which is only allowed on a loopback address.
.TP
.B ACC_WEBGUI_OPERATOR_USERS
Comma-separated users who get the operator tier; everyone else is a viewer.
Used when no group mapping is configured.
.TP
.BR ACC_WEBGUI_HTPASSWD_PATH ", " ACC_WEBGUI_SESSION_SECRET ", " ACC_WEBGUI_SESSION_TTL
For \fBhtpasswd\fR: the password file, the secret that signs session
cookies, and the session lifetime in seconds (default 43200, 12 hours).
.TP
.BR ACC_WEBGUI_OIDC_ISSUER ", " ACC_WEBGUI_OIDC_AUDIENCE ", " ACC_WEBGUI_OIDC_GROUPS_CLAIM
For \fBoidc\fR: the issuer, the expected audience, and the claim that
carries group membership (default \fBgroups\fR).
.TP
.B ACC_WEBGUI_GROUP_MAPPINGS
Maps identity-provider groups to the \fBviewer\fR, \fBoperator\fR and
\fBpublisher\fR tiers, for example
\fBoperator=acc\-operators;publisher=acc\-publishers,acc\-release\fR.
.TP
.BR ACC_WEBGUI_MTLS_HEADER ", " ACC_WEBGUI_MTLS_VERIFY_HEADER
For \fBmtls\fR: the headers a terminating proxy sets with the client
identity and the verification result.
\fBacc\-webgui\fR trusts them, so it must be reachable only through that
proxy.
.TP
.BR ACC_WEBGUI_OPERATOR_TOKEN ", " ACC_WEBGUI_VIEWER_TOKEN
For \fBtoken\fR: the bearer tokens for each role.
.TP
.B ACC_WEBGUI_STATIC_DIR
Serve the UI from this directory instead of the packaged one.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/acc/acc\-webgui.htpasswd.example
An example \fBhtpasswd\fR file.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
acc\-webgui                                  # local only, no login
acc\-deploy up \-\-webgui                       # as part of the stack
ACC_WEBGUI_HOST=0.0.0.0 ACC_WEBGUI_AUTH_MODE=htpasswd \e
  ACC_WEBGUI_HTPASSWD_PATH=/etc/acc/acc\-webgui.htpasswd acc\-webgui
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR acc (1),
.BR acc-tui (1),
.BR acc-deploy (1),
.BR htpasswd (1)
